  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> be an A.P. If the sum of its first four terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn></math> and the sum of its last four terms is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>170</mn></math> , then the product of its middle two terms is _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "754",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let the common difference of an A.P. be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>, then</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Also,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>170</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>170</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>32</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>170</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math></p><p>So, middle terms are&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>29</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>&#183;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>754</mn></math></p>"
  }
